# Frame and overlays: content that every page shows and a screen reader reads once, an Overlay plus a Page overlay with Pages: not-first.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Frame and overlays · Content on every page
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 40 40 40 40
	Styles:
		For style: ref
			Box:
				Width: 110
				Padding: 4 6
				Border: 1
				Border color: accent
			Typography:
				Size: 8
				Line height: 10
				Color: accent
				Align: right
	Section:
		Overlay:
			Offset: -30 0 auto auto
			Text: Receipt 2026-0147
				Style: ref
		Page overlay:
			Pages: not-first
			Offset: -30 0 auto auto
			Text: Receipt 2026-0147
				Style: ref
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Content on every page
		Paragraph: What a `Page overlay` holds is decoration and is not read. Data that must be seen on every page and also read goes twice: in an `Overlay` at the start of the section, which falls on the first page, and in a `Page overlay` with the same `Offset` and `Pages: not-first`.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: Both boxes have the page area as their reference container, so the reference of the receipt is in the same place on every page. A screen reader reads it once, at its place at the start of the section.
		Paragraph: The second page shows the copy from the Page overlay.
			Break:
				Before: page
